  "verbalization": "The compound (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan is implicated in the regulation of CCF-STTG1 through a series of molecular interactions. It acts as a target for multiple compounds, including 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide and Fructose 1,6-Diphosphate, which in turn target CCF-STTG1. This suggests a potential role for the compound in modulating the activity of CCF-STTG1, possibly through enzymatic pathways involving sialyltransferases and metabolic intermediates. The evidence is consistent with a mechanism where the compound influences the function of CCF-STTG1 via indirect pathways, possibly through the regulation of downstream metabolites or enzyme activity. The strength of the evidence is supported by multiple independent pathways, but the exact nature of the interaction remains partially uncertain, as the direct mechanism linking the compound to CCF-STTG1 is not fully elucidated.",
